tal event, like an app crash or the node being drained.\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. Fix the `get_nearby_events` result serialization (the rows are dropped) and the `search_logs` limit. Then rerun the ±60–300s window before 15:42:50.\n2. If you have the raw BGL file, run `grep 'R02-M1-N0-C:J12-U11' BGL.log | awk '$5 ~ /2005.06.03/'` and look at the lines before the first TLB error. In BGL, this pattern is often preceded by `ddr`/ECC or `machine check` messages."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":6196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df4b3611-8340-4544-ad4d-d2590684e91b","uuid":"9c97c108-c0d5-45a3-965d-51cf8964bd3b","timestamp":"2026-10-16T21:27:49.035Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6dCuDt79zDPUuy3m5ta"}
